      <!-- 1. Mechanism -->
      <article class="bg-[#0A1A12] border border-emerald-900/50 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xl">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-amber-400">1.</span> The Mechanism: Why Omega-7 Specifically
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          A healthy tear film has 3 layers: mucin (sticks tears to the eye), aqueous (water), and <strong class="text-amber-300">lipid (oil)</strong>. The lipid layer prevents evaporation — without it, tears vanish in 5 seconds. The meibomian glands behind your eyelids produce this oil, and they need <strong class="text-emerald-300">palmitoleic acid (Omega-7)</strong> as raw material. Fish oil (Omega-3) does not contain Omega-7. Sea buckthorn is the <em>only widely-available plant source</em> that does.
        </p>
